     26.300278,
     88.945278,
     "Dahagram"
    ]
   ],
   "s": "Until midnight on 31 July 2015, 102 pieces of India sat inside Bangladesh and 71 pieces of Bangladesh inside India, with 24 counter-enclaves inside those. One, Dahala Khagrabari, was a patch of India, inside Bangladesh, inside India, inside Bangladesh: 6,880 square metres of farmland. The swap gave Bangladesh 111 enclaves and India 51. Only Dahagram-Angarpota is left, joined to Bangladesh by the Tin Bigha Corridor."
  },
