   "s": "The Treaty of the Pyrenees of 1659 gave France the villages of the Cerdanya valley. Llívia was a town, so it stayed Spanish: 12.84 km² of Spain about 1.6 km inside France. This one is big enough for Natural Earth, which draws it at 13.2 km²."
  },
  {
