   "s": "Oman's Musandam peninsula, on the Strait of Hormuz, is cut off from the rest of Oman by the United Arab Emirates. Halfway between the two lies Madha, a piece of Oman surrounded by the Emirates, and inside Madha lies Nahwa, a village of about 40 buildings that belongs to Sharjah. The lines were settled in 1969. Natural Earth draws all three, Nahwa at 7.3 km²."
